==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-au-brush off.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb}}

# {{&lit|brush|off|lang=en}} To [[remove]] something with a [[brush]].
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[disregard]] (something), to [[dismiss]] or [[ignore]] (someone), as unimportant.
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Offing|chapter=XVIII|passage=Again I begged her to keep an eye on her blood pressure and not get so worked up, and once more she '''brushed me off''', this time with a curt request that I would go and boil my head.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} To [[depart]] with a sweeping motion.
#* Goldsmith
#*: Snatching his hat, he '''brushed''' off like the wind.

